WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.337
This CASE expression maps several known labels to standard categories.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:07.902
Electronics, electronic, and tech map to Electronics.

00:00:07.902 --> 00:00:13.937
Other documented variants map to their canonical labels.

00:00:13.937 --> 00:00:16.042
For a small teaching example, CASE is readable.

00:00:16.042 --> 00:00:23.912
For a larger production taxonomy, a reference or mapping table is usually easier to maintain.

00:00:23.912 --> 00:00:29.337
Standardization should make equivalent values comparable without inventing facts.

00:00:29.337 --> 00:00:37.102
Lowercasing an email or normalizing a known category map is different from guessing what an ambiguous value

00:00:37.102 --> 00:00:42.193
was supposed to mean. Good cleaning reduces representation noise while preserving uncertainty.
